SYSTEM(3)                      P32W Unix                       SYSTEM(3)

NAME
       system - run a shell command

SYNOPSIS
       #include <stdlib.h>

       int system(const char *cmd);

DESCRIPTION
       system runs cmd as /bin/sh -c cmd and waits for it to finish.
       Output buffered in the program's streams is written out
       first (fflush(NULL)), so it comes before the command's.
       While the command runs, the program ignores interrupt and
       quit, as the shell does for a command it waits for.

       system(NULL) asks whether there is a shell to run commands.

RETURN VALUE
       With cmd NULL, nonzero (P32W Unix always has /bin/sh).
       Otherwise the command's status as wait(2) gives it
       (WIFEXITED, WEXITSTATUS, WTERMSIG), or -1 if no process
       could be made. An exit status of 127 means the shell could
       not be run.

EXAMPLES
       if (system("cmp -s old new") == 0)
           printf("no change\n");

SEE ALSO
       popen(3), sh(1), fork(2), exec(2), wait(2)
